    "historical_decision": "Albanian Republic and Kingdom of Albania represent one continuous Albanian state identity across the 1 September 1928 constitutional change from republic to monarchy under the same ruler, Ahmet Zogu/Zog I. Contemporary U.S. diplomatic correspondence explicitly describes the Constituent Assembly as changing the form of government of Albania to a constitutional monarchy, while existing U.S.-Albanian legal arrangements continued in force. This supports a state-form transition rather than a state-identity rupture.",
